{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 24.2% a year from $1.70 billion in FY2016 to $12.0 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F196]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 step change, revenue up 49.1% to $6.21 billion, came from the U.S. launch of TRIKAFTA in the fourth quarter of 2019 and KAFTRIO in the EU in the third quarter of 2020 [F5][D194][P51]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2024 broke the trend with a $233 million operating loss, driven by $4.4 billion of non-deductible acquired in-process R&D from the Alpine acquisition [F24][P5][P11]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2025 recovered to $4.17 billion of operating income, but revenue growth slowed to 8.9% as TRIKAFTA/KAFTRIO grew only 0.7% [F25][D446][D530]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "TRIKAFTA/KAFTRIO supplied 85.9% of FY2025 revenue and contributed just 0.7pp of the 8.9% growth [D529][D531][D446]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "ALYFTREK, launched in FY2025, added 7.6pp of growth on $838 million of sales, or 7.0% of revenue [D590][S69][D589]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Net product revenues rose $950.5 million, or 9%, in FY2025 on continued demand, per the filing [P3][S39]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs fell 30.4% while revenue grew 8.9%, so incremental operating margin reached 449.1% [D457][D446][D463]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS rose to $15.32 from $13.89 while the diluted share count was flat at 258.0 million [F75][F73][X137][D459]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2025 operating margin of 34.8% sits above the 31.8% window median but below the 48.2% FY2022 high [F35][D663][D662]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The 36.9pp margin recovery was mostly a 37.7pp swing in other lines as the FY2024 acquired IPR&D charge did not repeat [D452][D468]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Cost of revenue held at 13.8% of revenue in FY2025 on a lower overall royalty rate for the CF medicines [D425][P4]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "SG&A rose 19.7%, cutting margin 1.3pp, while R&D grew 7.7% and added 0.4pp [D456][D467][D455][D466]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2024 effective tax rate of 315.5% reflected the non-deductible Alpine IPR&D; FY2025 normalized to 14.9% [D390][D433][P5]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating cash flow of $3.63 billion in FY2025 came primarily from $4.17 billion of income from operations [F85][F25][P1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow of $3.19 billion was 0.81x net income, below the 1.07x window median and the 1.11x peer median [F105][F45][D435][D675][D694]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex rose 47.0% to $438 million, 3.6% of revenue and 2.09x D&A [F95][D447][D430][D436]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Days inventory outstanding climbed to 373 days from 287, the working-capital drag on conversion [D444][D397]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cash and investments of $12.3 billion against no debt give net cash of 102.7% of revenue, the 88th percentile of eight biopharma peers [D438][D439][D440][D691]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Cash rose 9.8% in FY2025 primarily on increased cash and marketable securities from product revenue [D460][P2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $2.02 billion absorbed 63.2% of free cash flow, yet the diluted share count was unchanged [D441][D442][D459]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity of 22.5% trails the 38.7% peer median [D445][D696]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Days inventory outstanding rose 85 days to 373 in FY2025, a second straight large increase from 214 in FY2023 [D444][D397][D350]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Inventory is growing far faster than revenue, which ties up cash and risks write-downs if demand shifts [D462][D446]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 tax rate fell 300.7pp from the distorted FY2024 level, a base effect rather than a new concern [D433][D390][R2]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "FY2019 buybacks were later restated to $186.0 million from $192.0 million; the pack uses the first-reported figure [X141][R3]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "If TRIKAFTA/KAFTRIO growth stays near the FY2025 0.7% and ALYFTREK does not repeat its 7.6pp contribution, total growth would fall below the 8.9% level [D530][D590][D446]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "A further rise in days inventory outstanding above 373 days would confirm the working-capital drag on the 0.81x cash conversion [D444][D435]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin holding above the 31.8% window median in the FY2026 10-K would confirm the FY2025 recovery [D663][F35]."}
  ]}
]}
